1. **Noise Figure and Interference**:
   - **Compact Filters**: Smaller filters often have higher noise figures, making them more susceptible to interference from other satellites or ground-based sources. This can lead to reduced signal-to-noise ratios (SNRs) and decreased system performance.
   - **Phased Array Antennas**: While phased array antennas can mitigate noise and interference through beamforming and adaptive filtering techniques, the effectiveness of these methods depends critically on the quality and stability of the filters.

