Another example is SpaceX's Starlink constellation, which uses machine learning for beamforming and interference management. The system continually learns from the data it collects to optimize its performance and adapt to changing conditions.

In conclusion, while there are challenges in implementing AI and machine learning in real-world multi-beam satellite systems, these technologies offer significant potential for improving interference mitigation capabilities. By employing lightweight models, edge computing, and transfer learning, it is possible to overcome some of the challenges and achieve successful applications.

