The key technical challenge in designing hybrid SIW-waveguide feeding topologies for V-band satellite antennas is balancing efficiency and compactness. SIW offers high efficiency in small arrays but suffers from increased insertion loss as the array size grows. Waveguides provide low loss but are bulky. The hybrid approach optimizes performance by using SIW for smaller arrays and waveguides for larger ones, reducing overall size while maintaining high efficiency. This trade-off is crucial for V-band applications requiring both wideband operation and compact design.

