The hybrid approach addresses this issue by using SIW for smaller arrays and waveguides for larger ones. This allows for a reduction in overall size while maintaining high efficiency. The transition between SIW and waveguide is critical to ensure wide bandwidth and compact configuration. By optimizing the dimensions of the transition, designers can achieve a balance between efficiency and compactness, making the antenna suitable for V-band inter-satellite link applications.

