**New Insight:** Combining beamforming with advanced modulation schemes like 256-QAM or 1024-QAM can significantly enhance data rates in A2A links. Beamforming can focus the signal energy more precisely on the intended receiver, reducing interference and improving the Signal-to-Noise Ratio (SNR). This, in turn, allows for higher-order modulation schemes to be used effectively, increasing the data throughput. However, the complexity of implementing high-order modulation schemes increases with beamforming, as the system must handle multiple beams and ensure accurate signal alignment. Additionally, network coding can further improve reliability and throughput by encoding data across multiple beams, ensuring that even if some beams experience fading, the intended signal can still be decoded. The key challenge is optimizing the beamforming weights and coding schemes to work seamlessly together, balancing performance and computational complexity.

